# Class metaprogramming
-- the art of creating or customizing classes at runtime (most users don't need this, mainly for framework authors)
-- common way to dynamically create class, call type with 2 args:

  MyClass = type('Myclass', (Superclas, Mixin), {params})

-- avoid exec or eval for metaprogramming
-- you can use class decorators for customizing descriptors, but drawback: class decorators only act where they are directly applied

import time vs runtime
-- import time -- interpreter compiles function body, or class body to find syntax errors, lots of specifics (see page 689)
-- effects of class decorator might not affect subclasses 

Metaclasses
- metaclass is a class factory written as a class
- in python object model all classes are an instace of *type* (check Myclass.__class__)
- metaclasses also inherit (are subclasses of) from type, regular classes inherit from object
- when coding a metaclass, it is conventional to replace self with cls

How metaclasses are used: attribute validation, mass decorators to many methods at once, object serilaization or data conversion, orm, dynamic translation of class structures from other languages

